From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Sinyavin <sinyavin@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 20:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] usb: chipidea: qcom: add MDM9607 peripheral session

The selected ZTE MF283V factory DTB describes the USB controller as a
peripheral whose VBUS state is supplied by the PMIC, together with
qcom,dp-manual-pullup.  The downstream UDC translates a PMIC connect
notification into the GENCONFIG2/USBCMD session-valid override before
enabling the D+ pull-up.

The mainline qcom ChipIdea glue already implements the same session-valid
override for an extcon or role-switch source.  MDM9607 does not yet have
the corresponding PM8019 USB extcon path in mainline, so the controller
and UDC register but stay "not attached" even with a gadget bound.

Add an MDM9607-specific compatible which selects the existing
session-valid override and treats VBUS as active for this peripheral-only
controller. This deliberately does not add host mode or VBUS sourcing. A
future PM8019 VBUS provider can replace the fixed session state.

Signed-off-by: Dmitry Sinyavin <sinyavin@gmail.com>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/usb/ci-hdrc-usb2.yaml |  4 ++++
 drivers/usb/chipidea/ci_hdrc_msm.c             | 12 +++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/ci-hdrc-usb2.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/ci-hdrc-usb2.yaml
@@ -26,6 +26,9 @@ properties:
           - nxp,s32g2-usb
           - qcom,ci-hdrc
       - items:
+          - const: qcom,mdm9607-ci-hdrc
+          - const: qcom,ci-hdrc
+      - items:
           - enum:
               - nvidia,tegra114-ehci
               - nvidia,tegra124-ehci
--- a/drivers/usb/chipidea/ci_hdrc_msm.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/chipidea/ci_hdrc_msm.c
@@ -43,6 +43,7 @@ struct ci_hdrc_msm {
 	bool secondary_phy;
 	bool hsic;
 	void __iomem *base;
+	bool force_peripheral_session;
 };
 
 static int
@@ -114,7 +115,8 @@ static int ci_hdrc_msm_notify_event(stru
 			hw_write_id_reg(ci, HS_PHY_GENCONFIG_2,
 					HS_PHY_ULPI_TX_PKT_EN_CLR_FIX, 0);
 
-		if (!IS_ERR(ci->platdata->vbus_extcon.edev) || ci->role_switch) {
+		if (!IS_ERR(ci->platdata->vbus_extcon.edev) || ci->role_switch ||
+		    msm_ci->force_peripheral_session) {
 			hw_write_id_reg(ci, HS_PHY_GENCONFIG_2,
 					HS_PHY_SESS_VLD_CTRL_EN,
 					HS_PHY_SESS_VLD_CTRL_EN);
@@ -190,6 +192,12 @@ static int ci_hdrc_msm_probe(struct plat
 	ci->pdata.flags	= CI_HDRC_REGS_SHARED | CI_HDRC_DISABLE_STREAMING |
 			  CI_HDRC_OVERRIDE_AHB_BURST |
 			  CI_HDRC_OVERRIDE_PHY_CONTROL;
+	ci->force_peripheral_session =
+		of_device_is_compatible(pdev->dev.of_node,
+					"qcom,mdm9607-ci-hdrc");
+	if (ci->force_peripheral_session)
+		ci->pdata.flags |= CI_HDRC_FORCE_VBUS_ACTIVE_ALWAYS;
+
 	ci->pdata.notify_event = ci_hdrc_msm_notify_event;
 
 	reset = devm_reset_control_get(&pdev->dev, "core");
@@ -285,6 +293,7 @@ static void ci_hdrc_msm_remove(struct pl
 }
 
 static const struct of_device_id msm_ci_dt_match[] = {
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,mdm9607-ci-hdrc", },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,ci-hdrc", },
 	{ }
 };
